! TDDFT mode matrix 08/16 -- LR-PCM, NONEQUILIBRIUM solvation (default)
!
! The response kernel is built at the optical permittivity
! eps_inf = n^2 = 1.7756 while the ground state uses the static
! eps = 78.3553.  Adds the Kpcm(nov,nov) block to the solver phase.
!
! Physics check: singlets shift DOWN relative to the gas-phase case
! 06; triplets carry no direct solvent-response kernel and move only
! through the PCM ground-state orbitals.
%method  B3LYP
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%tddft   3
%tddft_multiplicity both
%pcm     cpcm
%solvent water
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
